# Zay local patch: vxfw Loop.zig Windows input-thread resilience.
# Upstream's ttyRun exits on the first console read error (swallowed by
# 'catch {}') and postEvent blocks forever on a full queue; either way the
# input thread dies/parks silently and ALL keyboard input stops while the
# app keeps rendering. Shutdown can also hang forever because a device-status
# query does not reliably wake Windows ReadConsoleInput. Use a dedicated
# cancellation event with WaitForMultipleObjects, use bounded retry +
# drop-with-warn, and keep exit diagnostics in ttyRun.
# See AGENTS.md 'vxfw Windows input-thread death' and build.zig checkVaxisPatches
# (patch list and required marker counts: tools/vendor-patches/manifest.txt).
# Re-apply after every `zig build --fetch` / vaxis bump; build.zig enforces this.
